From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Danil Somsikov <dsv@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 08:43:26 -0700
Subject: Disallow dot hosts and direct .headers file overrides in
 NetworkPersistenceManager

This prevents potential path traversal and unintended file creation in local overrides by:
- Rejecting http/https URLs with empty, '.', or '..' hosts in isForbiddenNetworkUrl and hasForbiddenPath.
- Encoding single dot ('.') path segments as '%2E' in encodeEncodedPathToLocalPathParts.
- Disallowing direct file saves for the .headers override file and guarding against empty override paths.

Bug: 562041808
Change-Id: I5a01b34b646ddc2150c2562ac91eccfb53e2db0a
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/devtools/devtools-frontend/+/8436055
Auto-Submit: Danil Somsikov <dsv@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Wolfgang Beyer <wolfi@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Wolfgang Beyer <wolfi@chromium.org>

